Where is Harry?

252
00:25:53,076 --> 00:25:56,037
It must be on the platform. Come on.

253
00:26:11,720 --> 00:26:15,223
Didn't your mom tell you
That it was rude to spy, Potter?

254
00:26:15,390 --> 00:26:16,975
<i>Petrificus Totalus!</i>

255
00:26:28,194 --> 00:26:29,654
Oh yes.

256
00:26:30,071 --> 00:26:33,366
He died before you could wipe the drool off.

257
00:26:38,872 --> 00:26:42,042
That's because of my father.
Enjoy the trip to London.

258
00:27:25,877 --> 00:27:27,629
<i>Finite!</i>

259
00:27:33,760 --> 00:27:35,053
- Hello, Harry.
- Moon!

260
00:27:35,428 --> 00:27:40,141
-How did you know where it was?
- Torposolos. You have a head full of them.

261
00:27:46,856 --> 00:27:49,526
I made you miss the carriages, Luna.

262
00:27:49,692 --> 00:27:52,862
No problem.
It was like being with a friend.

263
00:27:53,029 --> 00:27:55,073
I am your friend, Luna.

264
00:27:55,490 --> 00:27:57,283
How kind.

265
00:27:57,450 --> 00:28:00,662
It's about time!
I've been looking for them!

266
00:28:00,829 --> 00:28:03,665
That's right. Names?

267
00:28:03,915 --> 00:28:06,292
Professor Flitwick,
He has known me for 5 years.

268
00:28:06,459 --> 00:28:08,586
No exceptions, Potter.

269
00:28:09,129 --> 00:28:10,880
Who are they?

270
00:28:11,047 --> 00:28:13,341
<i>They are authors.
For security.</i>

271
00:28:13,508 --> 00:28:14,968
What is this rod for?

272
00:28:15,260 --> 00:28:17,512
It's not a rod, cretin. It's a cane!

273
00:28:17,679 --> 00:28:21,683
And why do you want a cane?

274
00:28:22,851 --> 00:28:25,937
This can be interpreted
as an offensive weapon.

275
00:28:26,104 --> 00:28:31,359
It's okay, Mr. Filch.
I can vouch for Mr. Malfoy.

276
00:28:38,741 --> 00:28:40,702
What a pretty face, Potter!

277
00:28:47,250 --> 00:28:49,586
Do you want me to fix it for you?

278
00:28:49,752 --> 00:28:53,548
I think you look more adventurous like this...

279
00:28:53,715 --> 00:28:55,258
...but as you want.

280
00:28:55,675 --> 00:28:57,969
Have you already fixed a nose?

281
00:28:58,136 --> 00:29:01,848
No, but I have fixed fingers
and there is not much difference.

282
00:29:04,309 --> 00:29:06,811
Well, yes. Treats.

283
00:29:09,230 --> 00:29:10,857
<i>EpiskeY-.</i>

284
00:29:17,405 --> 00:29:20,575
- How do I look?
- Extremely ordinary.

285
00:29:21,701 --> 00:29:23,077
Great.

286
00:29:30,460 --> 00:29:32,503
Don't worry, it will arrive in a minute.

287
00:29:36,382 --> 00:29:39,093
Do you want to stop eating?

288
00:29:39,260 --> 00:29:41,512
Your best friend disappeared!

289
00:29:42,889 --> 00:29:44,933
Ouch! Turn around, lunatic!

290
00:29:47,727 --> 00:29:49,229
He's covered in blood again.

291
00:29:49,854 --> 00:29:53,650
- Why is he always covered in blood?
- Looks like this time it's yours.

292
00:29:54,108 --> 00:29:55,985
Where were you?

293
00:29:56,152 --> 00:29:58,613
- What happened to your face?
- Then.

294
00:29:58,780 --> 00:30:00,406
What did I miss?

295
00:30:00,949 --> 00:30:04,744
The Sorting Hat asked
that we were brave.

296
00:30:04,911 --> 00:30:08,456
Easy for him to say, right?
It's a hat.

297
00:30:16,547 --> 00:30:19,217
- Very good night.
- Thank you.

298
00:30:21,427 --> 00:30:26,099
Let me introduce you
to the new faculty member...

299
00:30:26,266 --> 00:30:28,518
...Horace Slughorn.

300
00:30:32,397 --> 00:30:34,274
Professor Slughorn, I'm happy to say...

301
00:30:34,440 --> 00:30:38,736
...has agreed to resume his position
of potions master.

302
00:30:38,903 --> 00:30:41,823
The defense post
the dark arts...

303
00:30:41,990 --> 00:30:43,783
...will be occupied by Professor Snape.

304
00:30:44,200 --> 00:30:45,660
Snape?

305
00:30:51,708 --> 00:30:53,334
As you know...

306
00:30:53,501 --> 00:30:57,171
...you all were
registered upon arrival.

307
00:30:57,338 --> 00:30:59,340
They have the right to know why.

308
00:31:00,133 --> 00:31:03,720
Once we had a young man who,
like you...

309
00:31:03,886 --> 00:31:06,347
...sat in this very room...

310
00:31:06,723 --> 00:31:11,352
...he walked through the corridors of the castle,
He slept under this roof.

311
00:31:11,936 --> 00:31:16,316
It seemed to everyone
a student like any other.

312
00:31:16,482 --> 00:31:18,026
Your name?

313
00:31:19,485 --> 00:31:20,820
Tom Riddle.

314
00:31:25,992 --> 00:31:27,660
Today, naturally...

315
00:31:28,202 --> 00:31:31,539
...is known all over the world
by another name.

316
00:31:32,707 --> 00:31:37,920
That's why, as I'm watching them tonight...

317
00:31:38,087 --> 00:31:40,465
...I remember a very serious fact.

318
00:31:41,632 --> 00:31:44,761
Every day, at all hours...

319
00:31:44,927 --> 00:31:46,888
...maybe this very minute...

320
00:31:47,055 --> 00:31:51,392
...dark forces try to penetrate
inside this castle.

321
00:31:53,019 --> 00:31:58,566
But in the end his weapon
greater are you.

322
00:32:01,611 --> 00:32:03,738
It's something to think about.

323
00:32:04,989 --> 00:32:06,574
Now, to bed! Hurry up!

324
00:32:08,242 --> 00:32:10,036
It boosted our morale.

325
00:32:15,333 --> 00:32:20,088
History of Magic is up,
ladies, not below.

326
00:32:20,880 --> 00:32:25,885
Mr. Davies! That's the girls' bathroom.

327
00:32:28,679 --> 00:32:30,098
Potter.

328
00:32:31,432 --> 00:32:33,393
This can't be good.

329
00:32:36,687 --> 00:32:38,064
Are we having fun?

330
00:32:38,981 --> 00:32:42,193
- I had a free period this morning.
- I already realized.

331
00:32:42,693 --> 00:32:45,113
You might want to use it in potions.

332
00:32:45,279 --> 00:32:47,949
Do you no longer aspire to be an Auror?

333
00:32:48,741 --> 00:32:52,370
Yes, but I needed to get out
Extraordinary in the OWL.

334
00:32:52,537 --> 00:32:55,415
Yes, when Professor Snape
He taught potions.

335
00:32:55,581 --> 00:33:00,169
But Professor Slughorn
is accepting NEWT students...

336
00:33:00,336 --> 00:33:02,130
...with Exceed Expectations.

337
00:33:02,630 --> 00:33:04,132
Fantastic.

338
00:33:04,465 --> 00:33:06,926
- I'll go straight there.
- Very good.

339
00:33:07,093 --> 00:33:12,014
Take Weasley.
He's too happy there.

340
00:33:13,808 --> 00:33:15,101
I don't want to study potions.

341
00:33:15,268 --> 00:33:17,979
Quidditch tests are coming.
I need to practice.

342
00:33:19,230 --> 00:33:23,651
Attention to details
It is the prerequisite of all planning.

343
00:33:26,696 --> 00:33:30,616
I was already getting worried.
I see we brought someone.

344
00:33:31,242 --> 00:33:32,452
Ron Weasley, sir.

345
00:33:32,994 --> 00:33:35,455
But I'm terrible at potions,
a threat.

346
00:33:35,621 --> 00:33:37,665
- So I'm going to...
- Nonsense, you're going to learn.

347
00:33:37,832 --> 00:33:40,960
Any friend of Harry
He is my friend. His books.

348
00:33:41,127 --> 00:33:43,671
Sorry, I don't have my book yet,
nor did Ron either.

349
00:33:43,838 --> 00:33:45,548
Take what you want from the closet.

350
00:33:45,715 --> 00:33:49,051
As I told you, I prepared
some mixes this morning.

351
00:33:49,218 --> 00:33:53,181
Do you have any idea what they could be?

352
00:33:54,682 --> 00:33:57,268
- Yes, miss...?
- Granger, sir.

353
00:34:00,521 --> 00:34:04,984
That's veritaserum.
It is a serum that makes you tell the truth.

354
00:34:05,151 --> 00:34:07,862
And that's a polyjuice potion.

355
00:34:11,491 --> 00:34:13,159
It is very difficult to do it.

356
00:34:13,326 --> 00:34:15,369
And this is Amortentia.

357
00:34:15,536 --> 00:34:17,955
The love potion
most powerful in the world.

358
00:34:18,873 --> 00:34:22,710
It is said that it smells different for each
person, according to what attracts them.

359
00:34:24,003 --> 00:34:26,005
For example, I smell...

360
00:34:26,756 --> 00:34:30,801
...freshly mown grass
and new parchment and...

361
00:34:30,968 --> 00:34:34,305
...mint toothpaste.

362
00:34:35,723 --> 00:34:39,185
Amortentia does not create true love.
That's impossible.

363
00:34:39,352 --> 00:34:44,357
But if it causes a crush
temporary or an obsession.

364
00:34:44,524 --> 00:34:51,197
And that's why maybe it's the potion
most dangerous in this room.

365
00:34:56,744 --> 00:34:59,539
Sir? He hasn't told us what that one contains.

366
00:34:59,914 --> 00:35:01,624
Oh yes.

367
00:35:01,791 --> 00:35:04,377
What you see before you,
ladies and gentlemen...

368
00:35:04,544 --> 00:35:09,966
...it's a curious little potion
called Felix Felicis.

369
00:35:10,383 --> 00:35:12,635
But it is better known as...

370
00:35:12,802 --> 00:35:18,099
- Liquid luck.
- Yes, Miss Granger. Liquid luck.

371
00:35:18,599 --> 00:35:21,602
Very difficult to do,
disastrous if it goes wrong.

372
00:35:22,395 --> 00:35:27,400
One drink and they will achieve
everything they propose.

373
00:35:29,443 --> 00:35:31,946
At least until the effects wear off.

374
00:35:32,780 --> 00:35:36,617
This is what I'm telling you
to offer to everyone today.

375
00:35:36,784 --> 00:35:41,622
A little bottle of luck
liquid to the student who...

376
00:35:41,789 --> 00:35:46,377
...can make an acceptable sample
from “Dead in Life”.

377
00:35:46,544 --> 00:35:49,797
The recipe is on page 10 of your books.

378
00:35:49,964 --> 00:35:53,634
However, I inform you that...

379
00:35:53,801 --> 00:35:57,138
...only one student has managed to do
a potion worthy of this award.

380
00:35:57,805 --> 00:35:59,974
But good luck to everyone.

381
00:36:00,850 --> 00:36:02,643
Que empiece la cocción.

382
00:36:06,188 --> 00:36:08,816
Este libro es propiedad
del Príncipe Mestizo

383
00:36:28,836 --> 00:36:31,881
Instructions:
1) Cut a grain of sopophore.

384
00:36:32,048 --> 00:36:34,508
Moler con navaja
suelta mejor el jugo

385
00:36:38,471 --> 00:36:40,306
¿Cómo hiciste eso?

386
00:36:40,848 --> 00:36:43,017
Muélelo. No lo cortes.

387
00:36:43,184 --> 00:36:45,686
No. Las instrucciones
dicen que lo cortes.

388
00:36:45,853 --> 00:36:47,688
No, really.

389
00:37:12,546 --> 00:37:15,132
Only the 13 grain juice is used.

390
00:37:25,184 --> 00:37:28,354
By Merlin's beard!
¡Quedó perfecto!

391
00:37:29,855 --> 00:37:33,067
So perfect that a drop
nos mataría a todos.

392
00:37:36,362 --> 00:37:38,322
Here you are, as I promised.

393
00:37:38,489 --> 00:37:41,701
A little bottle of Felix Felicis.

394
00:37:41,867 --> 00:37:43,911
Congratulations.

395
00:37:44,412 --> 00:37:47,164
Úsalo sabiamente.

396
00:38:14,775 --> 00:38:17,445
Recibiste mi mensaje. Happens.

397
00:38:19,113 --> 00:38:20,489
How are you?

398
00:38:20,656 --> 00:38:22,199
Estoy bien, señor.

399
00:38:22,366 --> 00:38:23,617
Enjoying your classes?

400
00:38:24,869 --> 00:38:27,913
El profesor Slughorn
He is very impressed with you.

401
00:38:28,622 --> 00:38:30,916
I think you overestimate my abilities.

402
00:38:31,625 --> 00:38:32,752
Oh yeah?

403
00:38:33,294 --> 00:38:34,795
Definitivamente.

404
00:38:36,589 --> 00:38:39,383
How are your activities going outside of class?

405
00:38:40,593 --> 00:38:42,595
- Sir?
- I've noticed that you spend a lot of time...

406
00:38:42,762 --> 00:38:45,389
...con la Srta. Granger.

407
00:38:45,556 --> 00:38:46,807
Estaba pensando sí...

408
00:38:46,974 --> 00:38:51,979
No, no! Es muy inteligente
and we are friends, but no.

409
00:38:52,146 --> 00:38:55,149
Forgive me. I was just curious.

410
00:38:56,233 --> 00:38:58,110
But enough talk.

411
00:38:58,319 --> 00:39:01,906
You must wonder why
te pedí que vinieras.

412
00:39:02,490 --> 00:39:05,326
The answer lies here.

413
00:39:06,327 --> 00:39:08,496
What you are seeing are memories.

414
00:39:08,662 --> 00:39:12,500
In this case, one related
with an individual, Voldemort...

415
00:39:12,666 --> 00:39:15,127
...or, as it was known then,
Tom Riddle.

416
00:39:18,172 --> 00:39:22,009
Este frasquito contiene
a very particular memory...

417
00:39:22,176 --> 00:39:24,386
...from the day I met him.

418
00:39:25,721 --> 00:39:28,516
Quisiera que lo vieras,
si me haces el favor.

419
00:40:06,136 --> 00:40:09,223
<i>Your letter confused me a little,
Sr. Dumbledore.</i>

420
00:40:09,390 --> 00:40:10,391
ORFANATO DE WOOL

421
00:40:10,724 --> 00:40:14,186
Tom nunca ha recibido
visitas de un familiar.

422
00:40:14,353 --> 00:40:18,107
There have been very unpleasant incidents
con los otros niños.

423
00:40:20,526 --> 00:40:22,695
Tom, tienes visita.

424
00:40:23,237 --> 00:40:24,905
¿Cómo estás, Tom?

425
00:40:32,413 --> 00:40:33,664
No.

426
00:40:41,463 --> 00:40:44,592
- You are the doctor, right?
- No.

427
00:40:44,758 --> 00:40:46,802
Yo soy un profesor.

428
00:40:47,511 --> 00:40:49,346
No le creo.

429
00:40:49,513 --> 00:40:51,515
She wants me to be examined.

430
00:40:52,099 --> 00:40:54,310
They think I'm...different.

431
00:40:54,476 --> 00:40:55,978
Quizá tengan razón.

432
00:40:56,145 --> 00:40:57,605
I'm not crazy.

433
00:40:57,771 --> 00:41:01,108
Hogwarts is not a madhouse.

434
00:41:01,275 --> 00:41:03,277
Hogwarts is a school.

435
00:41:04,028 --> 00:41:05,195
A school of magic.

436
00:41:09,700 --> 00:41:12,453
You can do things, can't you, Tom?

437
00:41:13,579 --> 00:41:16,248
Things other children can't do.

438
00:41:17,625 --> 00:41:20,586
I can move things without touching them.

439
00:41:21,503 --> 00:41:25,090
I can make animals
do things without training them.

440
00:41:25,883 --> 00:41:29,428
I can make bad things happen to you
to the people who mistreat me.

441
00:41:30,054 --> 00:41:32,014
I can cause them pain...

442
00:41:32,640 --> 00:41:34,183
...if I want.

443
00:41:34,725 --> 00:41:36,602
Who are you?

444
00:41:36,769 --> 00:41:38,979
I'm like you, Tom.

445
00:41:40,147 --> 00:41:41,607
I am different.

446
00:41:42,650 --> 00:41:44,068
Prove it.

447
00:41:51,659 --> 00:41:55,496
I think there's something in your wardrobe
who wants to get out.

448
00:42:05,214 --> 00:42:09,009
At Hogwarts we do not tolerate theft.

449
00:42:09,176 --> 00:42:14,848
At Hogwarts we will not only teach you
to use magic, but to control it.

450
00:42:15,015 --> 00:42:16,183
Do you understand me?

451
00:42:20,145 --> 00:42:22,690
I can also talk to snakes.

452
00:42:23,941 --> 00:42:25,734
They look for me.

453
00:42:26,735 --> 00:42:28,654
They whisper things to me.

454
00:42:28,904 --> 00:42:32,032
Is that normal for someone like me?

455
00:42:53,095 --> 00:42:56,390
Did you know that, sir?
So?

456
00:42:56,557 --> 00:43:02,187
What was the most dangerous dark wizard
of history? No.

457
00:43:02,771 --> 00:43:04,898
If I had known, I...

458
00:43:06,525 --> 00:43:08,986
Through your time here,
at Hogwarts...

459
00:43:09,153 --> 00:43:12,489
...Tom Riddle got attached
from a particular teacher.

460
00:43:12,656 --> 00:43:14,491
Can you guess whose?

461
00:43:17,411 --> 00:43:20,873
He didn't bring Slughorn alone
to teach potions, right?

462
00:43:21,040 --> 00:43:23,083
No, it's true.

463
00:43:23,250 --> 00:43:27,087
Professor Slughorn owns something
that I intensely desire.

464
00:43:28,088 --> 00:43:29,965
And he won't give it to me easily.

465
00:43:30,132 --> 00:43:33,343
You said that the teacher
will try to collect me.

466
00:43:33,510 --> 00:43:34,762
That's right.

467
00:43:35,471 --> 00:43:37,473
Do you want me to allow it?

468
00:43:38,849 --> 00:43:40,225
Yes.

469
00:45:04,393 --> 00:45:06,103
Well...

470
00:45:06,270 --> 00:45:09,356
I'm going to ask you to do
some exercises...

471
00:45:09,523 --> 00:45:11,650
...to determine your strengths.

472
00:45:12,359 --> 00:45:14,361
Silence! Please!

473
00:45:14,528 --> 00:45:15,696
Shut up!

474
00:45:19,533 --> 00:45:21,618
Thank you. Very good.

475
00:45:22,452 --> 00:45:24,580
Even if they were
on the team last year...

476
00:45:24,746 --> 00:45:27,708
...that doesn't guarantee you a place this year.

477
00:45:30,210 --> 00:45:31,503
Very good.

478
00:45:40,220 --> 00:45:42,431
Don't take this the wrong way, Weasley.

479
00:45:42,973 --> 00:45:44,183
Don't take it the wrong way?

480
00:45:44,349 --> 00:45:47,895
I also want to be a guardian.
I like you.

481
00:45:48,061 --> 00:45:50,731
Really?
Someone as beefy as you?

482
00:45:50,898 --> 00:45:53,483
You have more of a body
of a hitter, right?

483
00:45:53,650 --> 00:45:56,570
The guardian needs to be fast, agile.

484
00:45:57,446 --> 00:45:59,239
I have good chances.

485
00:45:59,406 --> 00:46:03,202
Do you think you could introduce me
to your friend Granger?

486
00:46:03,368 --> 00:46:07,539
I would like to get to know her better,
if you understand me.

487
00:46:19,843 --> 00:46:21,553
Come on, Ron! Come on!

488
00:46:28,018 --> 00:46:29,269
Come on, Cormac!

489
00:46:45,786 --> 00:46:47,871
Come on, Ron!

490
00:46:56,171 --> 00:46:57,798
Come on, Ron.

491
00:46:58,548 --> 00:47:00,425
Come on, Ron.

492
00:47:18,318 --> 00:47:19,486
<i>Confundus.</i>

493
00:47:35,585 --> 00:47:37,921
Isn't it amazing?

494
00:47:40,674 --> 00:47:44,177
I thought I was going to be the last one.

495
00:47:44,511 --> 00:47:47,306
Hopefully Cormac doesn't take it too badly.

496
00:47:47,723 --> 00:47:50,767
He's a little interested in you,
Hermione. To Cormac.

497
00:47:51,852 --> 00:47:53,854
It's vile.

498
00:47:58,817 --> 00:48:01,069
Have you heard of this spell?
Sectumsempra?

499
00:48:01,236 --> 00:48:03,322
No, I haven't heard of him.

500
00:48:03,488 --> 00:48:06,616
And if you had a little honor,
You would return that book.

501
00:48:06,783 --> 00:48:09,244
It's unlikely.
He is the first in the class.

502
00:48:09,411 --> 00:48:13,582
He's even better than you.
Slughorn considers him a genius.

503
00:48:14,708 --> 00:48:16,001
What?

504
00:48:16,835 --> 00:48:19,546
I want to know who
