01:10:23,661 --> 01:10:26,538
I think she went to put on makeup.

756
01:10:26,705 --> 01:10:28,791
Your friend is an elusive flirt.

757
01:10:28,957 --> 01:10:31,669
And you like to exercise your mouth, right?

758
01:10:34,713 --> 01:10:36,715
What am I eating?

759
01:10:37,883 --> 01:10:39,510
Dragon balls.

760
01:10:50,729 --> 01:10:53,857
you just won
one month in detention, McLaggen.

761
01:10:54,024 --> 01:10:57,903
Not so fast, Potter.

762
01:10:59,446 --> 01:11:02,574
I need to rejoin
to the party. My friend...

763
01:11:02,741 --> 01:11:06,662
Can bear your absence
one more minute.

764
01:11:06,829 --> 01:11:09,081
Also, I just wish
transmit a message.

765
01:11:09,707 --> 01:11:11,959
- A message?
- From Professor Dumbledore.

766
01:11:12,126 --> 01:11:15,796
He sends you greetings and wishes you
May you enjoy the holidays.

767
01:11:15,963 --> 01:11:17,506
You will see...

768
01:11:17,673 --> 01:11:23,220
...he went on a trip. And it won't come back
until classes resume.

769
01:11:23,387 --> 01:11:24,930
Where did you go on a trip?

770
01:11:33,063 --> 01:11:34,940
Don't touch me, you filthy squib!

771
01:11:36,066 --> 01:11:37,776
Professor Slughorn, sir.

772
01:11:37,943 --> 01:11:42,281
I discovered this boy wandering
through an upstairs corridor.

773
01:11:42,448 --> 01:11:44,491
She said she had invited him to her party.

774
01:11:44,658 --> 01:11:47,953
Okay, I got in
without invitation! Glad?

775
01:11:48,120 --> 01:11:51,957
I'll escort him out.

776
01:11:54,752 --> 01:11:58,422
Of course, professor.

777
01:12:02,050 --> 01:12:05,304
Keep enjoying the party!

778
01:12:07,389 --> 01:12:12,311
Maybe I did curse the Bell girl.
Maybe not. What do you care?

779
01:12:12,478 --> 01:12:14,563
I swore to protect you.

780
01:12:14,730 --> 01:12:18,066
I took the unbreakable oath.

781
01:12:18,233 --> 01:12:20,402
I don't need protection.

782
01:12:20,569 --> 01:12:24,740
He chose me for this.
Of all of them. Me!

783
01:12:25,657 --> 01:12:29,203
- And I will not fail you.
- You're scared, Draco.

784
01:12:29,787 --> 01:12:33,707
You try to hide it, but it's obvious.
Let me help you.

785
01:12:33,874 --> 01:12:35,334
Nope!

786
01:12:35,667 --> 01:12:39,087
I was chosen! This is my moment!

787
01:12:51,517 --> 01:12:53,101
“The unbreakable oath”?

788
01:12:53,268 --> 01:12:54,895
Are you sure that's what Snape said?

789
01:12:55,062 --> 01:12:57,356
Completely. Because?

790
01:12:57,523 --> 01:13:01,026
You can't violate an oath
unbreakable.

791
01:13:01,193 --> 01:13:04,530
How curious, I had deduced the same thing.

792
01:13:05,030 --> 01:13:06,782
You don't understand.

793
01:13:07,407 --> 01:13:08,450
Demon.

794
01:13:36,270 --> 01:13:38,230
I miss you.

795
01:13:39,940 --> 01:13:41,483
Charming.

796
01:13:41,650 --> 01:13:44,945
He just wants to kiss me.
I have chapped lips. Look at me.

797
01:13:45,112 --> 01:13:47,322
I believe you.

798
01:13:57,416 --> 01:14:02,379
What happens to you if you break up
an unbreakable oath?

799
01:14:02,921 --> 01:14:04,631
You die.

800
01:14:10,053 --> 01:14:11,096
The pudding is still here.

801
01:14:12,347 --> 01:14:15,684
Did Voldemort choose Draco Malfoy?
for a mission?

802
01:14:15,851 --> 01:14:16,935
Yes, it seems crazy.

803
01:14:17,102 --> 01:14:20,606
Has Snape not pretended
offer help to Malfoy...

804
01:14:20,772 --> 01:14:23,275
...to find out what he was bringing?

805
01:14:23,442 --> 01:14:26,445
- I didn't get that impression.
- Maybe Harry is right.

806
01:14:26,987 --> 01:14:28,614
Take an unbreakable oath...

807
01:14:28,780 --> 01:14:32,284
It all comes down to whether you trust
in Dumbledore's opinion.

808
01:14:32,451 --> 01:14:34,703
If Dumbledore trusts
on Snape, me too.

809
01:14:34,870 --> 01:14:36,538
Dumbledore can make mistakes.

810
01:14:36,705 --> 01:14:37,873
Hatred blinds you.

811
01:14:38,040 --> 01:14:40,083
'No!
'SL te C!
99a!

812
01:14:41,835 --> 01:14:44,838
There are people disappearing every day.

813
01:14:45,005 --> 01:14:46,965
We can only trust
in a handful of people.

814
01:14:47,132 --> 01:14:50,093
If we fight among ourselves
we are lost

815
01:15:14,576 --> 01:15:16,119
Open your mouth.

816
01:15:17,788 --> 01:15:19,414
Don't you trust me?

817
01:15:25,671 --> 01:15:26,755
It's rich.

818
01:15:27,673 --> 01:15:30,509
I'm just going to... yeah.

819
01:15:37,265 --> 01:15:40,060
- A cupcake?
- For me, no.

820
01:15:51,989 --> 01:15:53,532
You have to forgive Remus.

821
01:15:53,782 --> 01:15:56,618
His illness upsets him.

822
01:15:57,536 --> 01:15:59,579
Do you Okay, Mr. Weasley?

823
01:15:59,746 --> 01:16:02,290
They are following us all.

824
01:16:02,457 --> 01:16:04,960
Molly rarely leaves the house.

825
01:16:05,794 --> 01:16:07,879
It hasn't been easy.

826
01:16:09,881 --> 01:16:11,299
Did you receive my Iechuza?

827
01:16:11,466 --> 01:16:13,552
Yes, I received it.

828
01:16:15,053 --> 01:16:18,098
If Dumbledore went on a trip,
The ministry doesn't know...

829
01:16:18,265 --> 01:16:20,726
...but maybe Dumbledore wants it that way.

830
01:16:21,435 --> 01:16:23,937
As for Draco Malfoy...

831
01:16:24,563 --> 01:16:25,731
...I know a little more.

832
01:16:26,356 --> 01:16:29,401
- Continue.
- I sent an agent to Borgin and Burke's.

833
01:16:29,568 --> 01:16:31,903
I think, from what you described to me...

834
01:16:32,070 --> 01:16:33,739
...than what you and Ron saw...

835
01:16:33,905 --> 01:16:37,409
...the object in which Draco
he is so interested...

836
01:16:37,576 --> 01:16:39,077
...it is an evanescent closet.

837
01:16:39,953 --> 01:16:41,246
An evanescent closet?

838
01:16:41,413 --> 01:16:45,417
They were in fashion when Voldemort
rose to power.

839
01:16:45,584 --> 01:16:48,545
The appeal is obvious.
If the Death Eaters came...

840
01:16:48,712 --> 01:16:53,467
...one would only have to get involved
and disappear for an hour or two.

841
01:16:54,092 --> 01:16:55,844
They can transport you anywhere.

842
01:16:56,011 --> 01:16:59,389
But they are deceptive,
very temperamental.

843
01:16:59,556 --> 01:17:02,476
What happened to Borgin and Burke's?

844
01:17:02,642 --> 01:17:03,769
Nothing.

845
01:17:04,603 --> 01:17:06,313
Still there.

846
01:17:17,532 --> 01:17:20,535
- It was delicious, Molly.
- Don't you want to stay?

847
01:17:20,702 --> 01:17:25,290
We have to go. the first night
of the cycle is the worst.

848
01:17:25,457 --> 01:17:26,458
Remus?

849
01:17:35,300 --> 01:17:36,843
My life.

850
01:17:45,143 --> 01:17:46,895
Has Ron gone to bed yet?

851
01:17:47,813 --> 01:17:49,898
Not yet. No.

852
01:17:51,691 --> 01:17:53,026
Your soreness.

853
01:18:05,622 --> 01:18:07,499
Merry Christmas, Harry.

854
01:18:08,917 --> 01:18:10,460
Merry Christmas.

855
01:18:27,727 --> 01:18:30,021
'Harfih no!
'Remus!

856
01:18:39,865 --> 01:18:41,283
Ginny!

857
01:18:44,452 --> 01:18:49,124
<i>I killed Sirius Black!</i>

858
01:18:49,291 --> 01:18:51,543
are you coming for me?

859
01:18:52,627 --> 01:18:55,964
Can you catch me? Are you coming for me?

860
01:19:25,702 --> 01:19:27,078
Harry?

861
01:19:44,596 --> 01:19:46,264
<i>Fainting!</i>

862
01:20:09,120 --> 01:20:10,872
Harry!

863
01:20:24,386 --> 01:20:25,595
Ginny!

864
01:20:55,166 --> 01:20:56,668
Molly.

865
01:21:18,815 --> 01:21:19,858
DISAPPEARANCES CONTINUE

866
01:21:20,025 --> 01:21:21,359
They can catch you easily.

867
01:21:21,526 --> 01:21:25,655
You were lucky they didn't kill you.
Realize who you are.

868
01:21:25,822 --> 01:21:28,366
I know who I am, Hermione, now?

869
01:21:29,326 --> 01:21:30,535
Excuse me.

870
01:21:32,203 --> 01:21:35,540
Of course I'm going to wear it.

871
01:21:35,707 --> 01:21:37,876
You are my Won-Won!

872
01:21:39,878 --> 01:21:42,297
Excuse me, I have to go throw up.

873
01:22:00,065 --> 01:22:02,233
<i>How do you find out about these things?</i>

874
01:22:02,400 --> 01:22:05,445
<i>You know more than half the staff.</i>

875
01:22:11,076 --> 01:22:12,619
<i>Lord...</i>

876
01:22:13,078 --> 01:22:15,914
...is it true that Professor Merrythought
is he going to retire?

877
01:22:16,081 --> 01:22:18,875
If I knew, I couldn't tell you.

878
01:22:19,125 --> 01:22:23,296
Thanks for the pineapple.
It is my favorite fruit.

879
01:22:23,880 --> 01:22:26,174
But how did you know?

880
01:22:28,009 --> 01:22:29,594
By intuition.

881
01:22:33,765 --> 01:22:35,475
Heavens! Is it that late?

882
01:22:35,642 --> 01:22:39,312
Leave or Dippett will put us
everyone in detention.

883
01:22:43,441 --> 01:22:47,278
Hurry up. Don't let them see you outside
out of bed at odd hours.

884
01:22:49,197 --> 01:22:51,282
- Did you want to talk to me about something, Tom?
- Yes sir.

885
01:22:52,617 --> 01:22:55,453
I couldn't think of anyone else
who to go to

886
01:22:56,371 --> 01:23:01,376
The other teachers...
Well, they're not like you.

887
01:23:01,751 --> 01:23:04,796
They can misunderstand me.

888
01:23:04,963 --> 01:23:06,548
Continue.

889
01:23:07,340 --> 01:23:09,634
The other night I was in the library...

890
01:23:10,176 --> 01:23:12,387
...in the prohibited section...

891
01:23:13,138 --> 01:23:16,683
...and I read something strange,
about a strange type of magic.

892
01:23:17,600 --> 01:23:21,104
I thought maybe you could clarify what it is.

893
01:23:21,271 --> 01:23:24,065
It's called, as I understand it...

894
01:23:26,985 --> 01:23:28,153
Excuse me?

895
01:23:28,319 --> 01:23:31,906
I don't know anything about that stuff
and if I knew, I wouldn't tell you!

896
01:23:32,073 --> 01:23:36,870
Get out of here and don't
mention it again!

897
01:23:39,831 --> 01:23:40,999
Are you confused?

898
01:23:41,666 --> 01:23:43,168
I'd be surprised if not.

899
01:23:44,085 --> 01:23:46,838
I don't understand. What happened?

900
01:23:47,005 --> 01:23:50,675
This is perhaps the memory
most important thing I have.

901
01:23:51,009 --> 01:23:52,760
It's also a lie.

902
01:23:53,678 --> 01:23:55,472
This memory has been altered...

903
01:23:55,638 --> 01:24:00,018
...by the person to whom it belongs,
our friend Slughorn.

904
01:24:00,643 --> 01:24:02,645
Why did he alter his own memory?

905
01:24:02,812 --> 01:24:05,690
- I suspect he is ashamed of her.
- Because?

906
01:24:05,857 --> 01:24:07,358
Why? Exact.

907
01:24:08,151 --> 01:24:11,529
I asked you to approach the teacher
and you have done it.

908
01:24:11,696 --> 01:24:15,325
I want you to convince him to reveal
his true memory...

909
01:24:15,492 --> 01:24:17,035
...as you can.

910
01:24:17,202 --> 01:24:19,162
I don't know you that well, sir.

911
01:24:23,625 --> 01:24:26,544
This memory is everything.

912
01:24:27,045 --> 01:24:29,047
Without it, we are blind.

913
01:24:29,547 --> 01:24:33,176
Without him, we leave destiny
of our random world.

914
01:24:35,220 --> 01:24:37,055
You have no alternative.

915
01:24:38,264 --> 01:24:40,266
You must not fail.

916
01:24:48,358 --> 01:24:52,320
I recommend that you study
again the antidotes chapter.

917
01:24:52,487 --> 01:24:56,241
I will tell you more about bezoars
in the next class. Go now.

918
01:24:56,407 --> 01:24:58,910
Alys! Don't forget your rat tail.

919
01:25:05,583 --> 01:25:08,169
If he is the prince of potions
in person!

920
01:25:08,336 --> 01:25:10,255
What is this pleasure for?

921
01:25:11,422 --> 01:25:13,508
Sir, can I ask you something?

922
01:25:13,675 --> 01:25:15,927
Ask all you want, boy.

923
01:25:16,094 --> 01:25:19,097
The other day I was
in the prohibited section of...

924
01:25:19,264 --> 01:25:22,934
...the library and I read something
about a strange magic.

925
01:25:24,269 --> 01:25:26,938
Yes. What was that weird magic?

926
01:25:27,105 --> 01:25:30,441
I don't know. I don't remember the name
exactly.

927
01:25:30,608 --> 01:25:34,946
But is there some kind of magic
What can't we be taught?

928
01:25:37,115 --> 01:25:38,283
I am a potions master.

929
01:25:38,449 --> 01:25:41,286
You should ask Professor Snape.

930
01:25:41,452 --> 01:25:42,954
Yes.

931
01:25:43,538 --> 01:25:46,040
He and I don't get along very well.

932
01:25:46,207 --> 01:25:48,001
What I want to say is...

933
01:25:48,835 --> 01:25:50,628
...that he's not like you.

934
01:25:51,296 --> 01:25:53,131
Maybe you misunderstand me.

935
01:25:54,424 --> 01:25:58,261
Yes. There can be no light without darkness.

936
01:25:58,428 --> 01:26:02,473
The same with magic.
I try to live within the light.

937
01:26:03,099 --> 01:26:04,767
I suggest you do the same.

938
01:26:05,143 --> 01:26:08,146
That's what you said to Tom Riddle
When did you ask him questions?

939
01:26:15,111 --> 01:26:18,156
Dumbledore sent you as a detective, right?

940
01:26:20,158 --> 01:26:21,784
Isn't it true?

941
01:26:29,083 --> 01:26:30,460
Yes?

942
01:26:30,835 --> 01:26:32,962
Ah, it's you, Potter.

943
01:26:33,129 --> 01:26:35,506
Sorry. I'm busy
at this moment.

944
01:26:48,311 --> 01:26:52,106
It's beautiful, isn't it? The moon

945
01:26:53,107 --> 01:26:54,525
Divine.

946
01:26:55,193 --> 01:26:57,487
Did we have a late snack?

947
01:26:58,613 --> 01:27:02,200
The box was on your bed.
I decided to try one.

948
01:27:02,367 --> 01:27:05,870
- Or twenty.
- I can't stop thinking about her.

949
01:27:06,037 --> 01:27:08,039
I thought I was already bothering you.

950
01:27:08,206 --> 01:27:10,541
It's never going to bother me.

951
01:27:12,335 --> 01:27:13,878
I think I love her.

952
01:27:17,465 --> 01:27:19,759
Fantastic.

953
01:27:23,596 --> 01:27:25,223
Do you think he knows that I exist?

954
01:27:25,390 --> 01:27:27,892
You better. He's been kissing you for 3 months.

955
01:27:28,059 --> 01:27:31,020
Kissing me? Who are you talking about?

956
01:27:31,938 --> 01:27:33,189
Who are you talking about?

957
01:27:33,940 --> 01:27:37,568
From Romilda, of course. Romilda Vane.

958
01:27:37,735 --> 01:27:39,237
How funny.

959
01:27:42,365 --> 01:27:43,408
And why that?

960
01:27:43,574 --> 01:27:46,035
It's not a joke!
I'm in love with her!

961
01:27:46,202 --> 01:27:49,080
Well, you're in love.
Do you even know her?

962
01:27:50,039 --> 01:27:53,000
No. Can you introduce her to me?

963
01:28:14,689 --> 01:28:19,444
Come on, Ron.
I'm going to introduce you to Romilda Vane.

964
01:28:24,031 --> 01:28:25,074
Dear Harry

965
01:28:25,241 --> 01:28:28,619
You sweeten my heart Romilda

966
01:28:30,204 --> 01:28:33,916
Excuse me, I wouldn't bother you.
if it were not essential.

967
01:28:34,751 --> 01:28:36,169
Where is Romilda?

968
01:28:36,335 --> 01:28:38,296
What's wrong with Wenby?

969
01:28:38,796 --> 01:28:40,631
A very powerful love potion.

970
01:28:40,798 --> 01:28:43,176
Very good. They better come in.

971
01:28:43,342 --> 01:28:46,637
You should be able to do
a quick remedy for this.

972
01:28:46,804 --> 01:28:49,724
I thought it was needed
a more experienced hand.

973
01:28:49,891 --> 01:28:52,977
Hello, sweetheart. Do you want a drink?

974
01:28:53,144 --> 01:28:54,812
Maybe you're right.

975
01:28:59,317 --> 01:29:04,739
Excuse me for what happened earlier.
The misunderstanding.

976
01:29:04,906 --> 01:29:09,285
It was nothing.
What is past is past. TRUE?

977
01:29:09,452 --> 01:29:12,371
He must be fed up with it
after so many years.

978
01:29:12,538 --> 01:29:15,124
Of all the questions about Voldemort.

979
01:29:15,291 --> 01:29:17,126
Don't say that name!

980
01:29:24,842 --> 01:29:26,928
Here you go, boy. Take it.

981
01:29:27,094 --> 01:29:30,223
- What is this?
- A tonic for the nerves.

982
01:29:44,737 --> 01:29:47,031
- What happened to me?
- A love potion.

983
01:29:47,198 --> 01:29:49,325
And very strong, too.

984
01:29:49,909 --> 01:29:53,538
- I feel very bad.
- You need something to cheer you up.

985
01:29:53,704 --> 01:29:57,375
I have butterbeer,
wine, top-notch mead.

986
01:29:57,542 --> 01:30:01,879
I had it reserved for something else,
but given the circumstances...

987
01:30:04,173 --> 01:30:05,883
Here, Potter.

988
01:30:06,050 --> 01:30:07,552
For life!

989
01:30:12,348 --> 01:30:13,391
Ron!

990
01:30:15,852 --> 01:30:19,313
- Q. Ron!
r
l Ofessor! Do something!

991
01:30:20,398 --> 01:30:22,024
I don't understand!

992
01:30:38,416 --> 01:30:40,209
Come on, Ron, breathe!

993
01:31:02,440 --> 01:31:05,276
Those girls are going to kill me.

994
01:31:16,287 --> 01:31:19,665
Good idea using a bezoar, Harry.

995
01:31:19,832 --> 01:31:22,376
You must be very proud
of your student.

996
01:31:23,669 --> 01:31:25,796
Yes, very proud.

997
01:31:25,963 --> 01:31:28,716
We agree
that his actions were heroic.

998
01:31:28,883 --> 01:31:32,887
The question is:
Why were they necessary?

999
01:31:33,054 --> 01:31:34,639
Why? Exact.

1000
01:31:35,014 --> 01:31:36,974
This seems to be a gift, Horace.

1001
01:31:37,308 --> 01:31:40,144
Do you remember who gave you the bottle?

1002
01:31:40,311 --> 01:31:44,273
It has some subtle
nuances of orozuz and cherry...

1003
01:31:44,440 --> 01:31:46,901
...when it is not contaminated
with poison.

1004
01:31:47,068 --> 01:31:50,196
I intended to give him a gift.

1005
01:31:50,363 --> 01:31:51,739
Who, may I ask?

1006
01:31:53,574 --> 01:31:55,743
To you, Mr. Director.

1007
01:31:58,079 --> 01:31:59,163
Where is it?

1008
01:31:59,330 --> 01:32:03,459
Where's my Won-Won?
Have you been asking about me?

1009
01:32:06,504 --> 01:32:08,172
What is she doing here?

1010
01:32:08,339 --> 01:32:10,591
I ask you the same thing.

1011
01:32:10,758 --> 01:32:13,010
I'm his girlfriend!

1012
01:32:13,177 --> 01:32:15,930
I am your... friend.

1013
01:32:16,097 --> 01:32:20,309
Don't make me laugh.
They haven't spoken in weeks!

1014
01:32:21,102 --> 01:32:23,980
Do you want to make peace because
became very interesting?

1015
01:32:24,146 --> 01:32:27,858
They poisoned him, moron!

1016
01:32:28,025 --> 01:32:30,861
And I have always found it interesting.

1017
01:32:33,489 --> 01:32:37,576
See? Feel my presence!

1018
01:32:37,743 --> 01:32:41,038
Don't worry, Won-Won.
Here I am!

1019
01:32:41,706 --> 01:32:43,541
Here I am!

1020
01:32:49,380 --> 01:32:52,591
Hermione.

1021
01:32:56,637 --> 01:32:58,639
Hermione.

1022
01:32:59,390 --> 01:33:01,642
Hermione.

1023
01:33:09,233 --> 01:33:13,154
Who was young and felt
the crush of love.

1024
01:33:13,487 --> 01:33:15,823
Let's go, everyone.

1025
01:33:15,990 --> 01:33:18,617
Mr. Weasley is well cared for.

1026
01:33:22,872 --> 01:33:25,416
It's about time, don't you think?

1027
01:33:28,085 --> 01:33:29,670
Thank you.

1028
01:33:32,590 --> 01:33:34,425
Shut up.

1029
01:34:53,337 --> 01:34:56,757
BORGIN AND BURKE
Established in 1863

1030
01:35:46,724 --> 01:35:50,519
Stop it, Ron!
You're making it snow!

1031
01:35:54,982 --> 01:35:57,651
Explain to me how I broke up with Lavender.

1032
01:36:01,488 --> 01:36:04,491
He went to visit you at the hospital.

1033
01:36:05,367 --> 01:36:07,786
And you spoke.

1034
01:36:09,371 --> 01:36:13,459
It wasn't a conversation
particularly long.

1035
01:36:13,626 --> 01:36:16,921
Don't misunderstand me.
I'm glad we broke up.

1036
01:36:17,087 --> 01:36:19,423
But she seems very upset.

1037
01:36:25,930 --> 01:36:29,433
Yes, it seems that way, right?

1038
01:36:31,060 --> 01:36:36,106
You say you don't remember
nothing from that night?

1039
01:36:36,273 --> 01:36:39,276
Nothing at all?

1040
01:36:39,443 --> 01:36:41,278
Yes there is something.

1041
01:36:44,782 --> 01:36:49,245
But it can't be.
I was totally giddy, wasn't I?

1042
01:36:50,746 --> 01:36:53,958
Yes. Stunned.

1043
01:36:58,545 --> 01:37:01,048
Sectusempra. - For Enemies

1044
01:37:01,215 --> 01:37:02,466
Harry.

1045
01:37:03,926 --> 01:37:05,094
It's Katie.

1046
01:37:07,054 --> 01:37:08,681
Katie Bell.

1047
01:37:16,355 --> 01:37:18,732
Katie. How are you?

1048
01:37:19,400 --> 01:37:23,904
I know you're going to ask me,
but I don't know who cursed me.

1049
01:37:25,531 --> 01:37:29,076
I have been trying
to remember, really.

1050
01:37:29,493 --> 01:37:32,913
But I can't.

1051
01:37:46,176 --> 01:37:47,511
Katie?

1052
01:38:29,970 --> 01:38:34,058
I know what you did, Malfoy.
You put a spell on her, didn't you?

1053
01:39:04,421 --> 01:39:06,423
<i>Sectusempra!</i>

1054
01:39:53,387 --> 01:39:56,306
<i>Vulnera sanentur.</i>

1055
01:39:57,975 --> 01:40:00,811
<i>Vulnera sanentur.</i>

1056
01:40:03,105 --> 01:40:05,983
<i>Vulnera sanentur.</i>

1057
01:40:06,358 --> 01:40:10,446
MAKING ADVANCED POTIONS

1058
01:40:27,087 --> 01:40:30,632
You have to get rid of it. Today.

1059
01:40:35,512 --> 01:40:37,139
Give me your hand.

1060
01:40:53,113 --> 01:40:55,032
The Room of Requirement.

1061
01:41:01,497 --> 01:41:04,124
We need to hide the book
of the Half-Blood Prince...

1062
01:41:04,291 --> 01:41:08,003
...where no one can find it,
including you.

1063
01:41:16,345 --> 01:41:17,804
- What was that?
- What was that?

1064
01:41:43,914 --> 01:41:45,249
See?

1065
01:41:45,791 --> 01:41:47,834
You never know what you'll find here.

1066
01:42:06,979 --> 01:42:10,899
Close your eyes. So you can't
feel no temptation.

1067
01:42:14,736 --> 01:42:16,446
Close your eyes.

1068
01:42:43,140 --> 01:42:46,018
That can stay here too.

1069
01:43:00,657 --> 01:43:03,035
So you and Ginny did it?

1070
01:43:03,201 --> 01:43:04,369
What?

1071
01:43:04,536 --> 01:43:06,622
Did they hide the book?

1072
01:43:06,788 --> 01:43:08,665
Oh yes.

1073
01:43:12,502 --> 01:43:14,171
Oh dear, yes.

1074
01:43:14,338 --> 01:43:17,132
Have you still not had
Good luck with Slughorn?

1075
01:43:19,176 --> 01:43:20,510
Good luck.

1076
01:43:21,553 --> 01:43:24,890
That's it. I just need a little luck.

1077
01:43:43,033 --> 01:43:46,244
Tell us. How do you feel?

1078
01:43:46,411 --> 01:43:48,038
Excellent.

1079
01:43:49,206 --> 01:43:51,208
Truly excellent.

1080
01:43:53,960 --> 01:43:55,545
Remember...

1081
01:43:55,879 --> 01:43:57,631
...SIughorn usually eats early...

1082
01:43:57,798 --> 01:44:00,801
...takes a walk and then returns to his office.

1083
01:44:00,967 --> 01:44:02,469
True.

1084
01:44:02,886 --> 01:44:05,055
- I'm going to Hagrid's house.
- That?

1085
01:44:05,222 --> 01:44:07,891
No. Harry, you have to talk to Slughorn!

1086
01:44:09,476 --> 01:44:12,062
We have a plan.

1087
01:44:12,229 --> 01:44:14,314
I have a feeling what's going to happen
something good with Hagrid.

1088
01:44:14,481 --> 01:44:18,235
I feel like I should be there.
Do you understand me?

1089
01:44:19,111 --> 01:44:21,363
- No.
- Trust me. I know what I'm doing.

1090
01:44:21,530 --> 01:44:23,699
Or Felix knows.

1091
01:44:24,825 --> 01:44:26,326
Hello!

1092
01:44:56,940 --> 01:44:58,650
Merlin's beard, Harry!

1093
01:44:58,817 --> 01:45:02,946
Sorry. I should have announced myself.
Clearing throat or coughing.

1094
01:45:03,113 --> 01:45:05,073
must have feared
that it was Professor Sprout.

1095
01:45:05,240 --> 01:45:08,660
The truth is, yes. What made you think that?

1096
01:45:08,827 --> 01:45:10,912
His behavior in general.

1097
01:45:11,079 --> 01:45:13,874
Walking secretly, jumping when you see me.

1098
01:45:14,040 --> 01:45:17,627
And those Tentacula leaves?
They are very valuable, right?

1099
01:45:17,794 --> 01:45:20,130
Ten galleons a sheet
for certain buyers.

1100
01:45:20,297 --> 01:45:23,800
I don't know about those back alley purchases,
but one hears rumors.

1101
01:45:23,967 --> 01:45:27,763
my own interests
They are purely academic.

1102
01:45:27,929 --> 01:45:31,224
Those leaves scare me.

1103
01:45:34,478 --> 01:45:36,646
How did you get out of the castle?

1104
01:45:36,813 --> 01:45:38,315
Through the front door.

1105
01:45:38,482 --> 01:45:40,650
I'm going to Hagrid's house.
He is a good friend...

1106
01:45:40,817 --> 01:45:42,527
...and I wanted to see it.

1107
01:45:42,694 --> 01:45:44,988
So, with your permission, I withdraw.

1108
01:45:45,781 --> 01:45:47,407
Harry!

1109
01:45:48,241 --> 01:45:50,702
- Sir?
- It's almost dark!

1110
01:45:50,869 --> 01:45:54,331
I can't let you walk
walking outside alone.

1111
01:45:54,498 --> 01:45:57,083
Then come with me, sir.

1112
01:46:02,422 --> 01:46:07,552
I insist that you accompany me
back to the castle immediately!

1113
01:46:07,719 --> 01:46:10,972
That would be counterproductive, sir.

1114
01:46:12,307 --> 01:46:14,434
Why do you say it?

1115
01:46:15,519 --> 01:46:17,103
I have no idea.

1116
01:46:23,860 --> 01:46:25,278
Horace.

1117
01:46:25,904 --> 01:46:31,201
By Merlin's beard!
Is it a real acromantula?

1118
01:46:31,785 --> 01:46:33,870
A dead one, I think, sir.

1119
01:46:34,663 --> 01:46:36,206
Holy shit.

1120
01:46:36,832 --> 01:46:39,918
How did you manage to kill her?

1121
01:46:40,210 --> 01:46:43,672
To kill her? He was my oldest friend.

1122
01:46:43,839 --> 01:46:48,051
- I'm sorry, I didn't know...
- Don't worry, you're not the only one.

1123
01:46:48,552 --> 01:46:52,013
Spiders are creatures
Seriously misunderstood.

1124
01:46:52,180 --> 01:46:54,391
It's the eyes, I think.
They scare some people.

1125
01:46:54,808 --> 01:46:56,935
Let alone the tweezers.

1126
01:47:01,064 --> 01:47:03,024
Yeah, I guess that's it too.

1127
01:47:03,733 --> 01:47:07,112
I don't want to be insensitive...

1128
01:47:07,279 --> 01:47:11,366
...but acromantular venom
It is extremely rare.

1129
01:47:11,533 --> 01:47:13,743
Can you allow me to extract
one or two vials?

1130
01:47:13,910 --> 01:47:16,538
For academic purposes only, of course.

1131
01:47:16,705 --> 01:47:19,624
I guess not anymore
It's going to be very useful to you.

1132
01:47:19,791 --> 01:47:21,001
I thought the same.

1133
01:47:21,167 --> 01:47:27,674
I always bring a vial
for occasions like this.

1134
01:47:27,924 --> 01:47:32,929
Custom of an old man
potions master

1135
01:47:33,597 --> 01:47:36,057
I wish I had seen it when I was young.

1136
01:47:36,224 --> 01:47:39,895
It was magnificent. Simply magnificent.

1137
01:47:41,313 --> 01:47:42,898
Heavens.

1138
01:47:52,616 --> 01:47:55,827
- Do you want me to say a few words?
- Yes.

1139
01:47:56,077 --> 01:47:57,621
He had a family, I guess?

1140
01:47:57,787 --> 01:47:59,289
Oh yes.

1141
01:48:04,628 --> 01:48:06,129
See you...

1142
01:48:06,296 --> 01:48:08,173
Arag09-

1143
01:48:12,677 --> 01:48:15,597
See you, Aragog...

1144
01:48:15,972 --> 01:48:18,642
...king of the arachnids.

1145
01:48:19,476 --> 01:48:22,062
Your body will decompose...

1146
01:48:23,313 --> 01:48:26,149
...but your spirit
will remain among us.

1147
01:48:26,858 --> 01:48:33,323
And your friends will find solace
for the loss they had.

1148
01:48:48,672 --> 01:48:52,300
I had him since he was an egg.
He was very small when he came out.

1149
01:48:52,467 --> 01:48:56,179
He looked like a Pekingese.
A Pekingese, really.

1150
01:48:56,346 --> 01:49:01,518
How cute! I had a fish.
Francis. I loved him very much.

1151
01:49:01,685 --> 01:49:07,190
One afternoon I came down and he had disappeared.

1152
01:49:08,775 --> 01:49:11,987
- How strange, isn't it?
- Right?

1153
01:49:12,153 --> 01:49:15,865
But that's life, I guess.

1154
01:49:16,032 --> 01:49:21,371
You are alive, everything is normal,
and suddenly... poof!

1155
01:49:39,764 --> 01:49:42,892
A student gave me Francis.

1156
01:49:43,893 --> 01:49:48,189
One spring afternoon I discovered
a bowl on my desk...

1157
01:49:49,107 --> 01:49:52,068
...which contained only a few centimeters
of clean water.

1158
01:49:52,861 --> 01:49:56,406
And floating on the surface
there was the petal of a flower.

1159
01:49:57,949 --> 01:50:00,410
I stared at him and he sank.

1160
01:50:01,911 --> 01:50:04,497
Just before reaching the bottom...

1161
01:50:04,956 --> 01:50:06,374
...was transformed...

1162
01:50:07,751 --> 01:50:09,586
...in a little fish.

1163
01:50:11,254 --> 01:50:13,381
It was beautiful magic.

1164
01:50:14,382 --> 01:50:16,634
An amazing spectacle.

1165
01:50:19,262 --> 01:50:22,015
The flower petal came from a lily.

1166
01:50:24,392 --> 01:50:25,435
From your mother Lily.

1167
01:50:27,479 --> 01:50:29,981
The day I went down...

1168
01:50:30,940 --> 01:50:33,234
...the day the bowl was empty...

1169
01:50:34,778 --> 01:50:36,946
...it was the day your mother...

1170
01:50:40,950 --> 01:50:42,952
I know why you are here.

1171
01:50:45,955 --> 01:50:47,957
But I can't help you.

1172
01:50:49,751 --> 01:50:51,461
It would ruin me.

1173
01:50:55,173 --> 01:50:57,634
Do you know why I survived, Professor?

1174
01:50:58,176 --> 01:51:00,011
The night they did this to me?

1175
01:51:01,763 --> 01:51:03,389
For her.

1176
01:51:04,307 --> 01:51:06,101
Because she sacrificed herself.

1177
01:51:06,518 --> 01:51:08,895
Because he refused to step aside.

1178
01:51:09,062 --> 01:51:12,273
Because his love was more powerful
than Voldemort.

1179
01:51:12,440 --> 01:51:16,152
- Don't say his name.
- I'm not afraid of the name.

1180
01:51:16,986 --> 01:51:19,114
I'm going to tell you something.

1181
01:51:20,031 --> 01:51:22,992
Something that for others is mere conjecture.

1182
01:51:24,953 --> 01:51:26,454
It's true.

1183
01:51:27,038 --> 01:51:28,331
I am the Chosen One.

1184
01:51:29,332 --> 01:51:31,543
Only I can destroy it,
but to do it...

1185
01:51:31,709 --> 01:51:35,004
...I need to know what he asked you
Tom Riddle in his office...

1186
01:51:35,171 --> 01:51:37,549
...and I need to know what you told him.

1187
01:51:38,258 --> 01:51:40,677
Be brave, professor.

1188
01:51:42,303 --> 01:51:44,389
Be brave like my mother.

1189
01:51:45,682 --> 01:51:48,351
If not, disgrace.

1190
01:51:49,477 --> 01:51:51,771
If not, she will have died in vain.

1191
01:51:52,772 --> 01:51:57,986
If not, the bowl will remain empty,
forever.

1192
01:52:08,538 --> 01:52:11,666
Please don't think wrong
from me when you see it.

1193
01:52:13,668 --> 01:52:16,963
You have no idea what he was like,
even then.

1194
01:52:53,708 --> 01:52:56,419
The other night I was in the library...

1195
01:52:56,586 --> 01:52:58,755
...in the prohibited section...

1196
01:52:59,631 --> 01:53:03,259
...and I read something strange,
about a strange type of magic.

1197
01:53:04,552 --> 01:53:07,305
It's called, as I understand it...

1198
01:53:08,598 --> 01:53:09,933
...a horcrux.

1199
01:53:11,768 --> 01:53:14,520
- How do you say?
- Horcrux.

1200
01:53:14,938 --> 01:53:17,607
I discovered the term
when I was reading.

1201
01:53:17,774 --> 01:53:20,777
I didn't fully understand it.

1202
01:53:20,944 --> 01:53:25,448
I don't know what you were reading,
but these are very dark things.

1203
01:53:25,615 --> 01:53:27,158
That's why...

1204
01:53:28,284 --> 01:53:30,119
...that I came with you.

1205
01:53:32,956 --> 01:53:38,586
A horcrux is an object
in which someone hid part of their soul.

1206
01:53:38,753 --> 01:53:41,381
I don't understand how that works, sir.

1207
01:53:43,967 --> 01:53:47,971
One separates his soul and hides
part of it into an object.

1208
01:53:48,137 --> 01:53:51,766
By doing so you are protected if someone
It attacks you and destroys your body.

1209
01:53:51,933 --> 01:53:53,059
Protected?

1210
01:53:53,226 --> 01:53:56,437
The part of your soul that is
hidden is still alive.

1211
01:53:57,897 --> 01:54:00,316
In other words, you can't die.

1212
01:54:07,490 --> 01:54:10,660
And how does one divide his soul, sir?

1213
01:54:10,827 --> 01:54:13,621
I think you already know the answer, Tom.

1214
01:54:14,831 --> 01:54:16,332
Murdering.

1215
01:54:16,833 --> 01:54:18,167
Yes.

1216
01:54:18,710 --> 01:54:23,631
Killing breaks your soul.
It is a violation against nature.

1217
01:54:24,507 --> 01:54:29,262
Is the soul only separated once?
For example, if there were seven...?

1218
01:54:29,429 --> 01:54:30,930
Seven?

1219
01:54:31,681 --> 01:54:36,978
By Merlin's beard.
Isn't it bad to kill just one person?

1220
01:54:37,145 --> 01:54:40,898
Split the soul into seven pieces...

1221
01:54:42,066 --> 01:54:45,111
It's all hypothetical, right? Academic?

1222
01:54:49,866 --> 01:54:51,200
Of course, sir.

1223
01:54:54,162 --> 01:54:56,164
It will be our little secret.

1224
01:55:04,964 --> 01:55:06,215
<i>Sir.</i>

1225
01:55:21,606 --> 01:55:23,733
This is worse than what I had
imagined.

1226
01:55:23,900 --> 01:55:26,569
So it was successful?
Did you manage to make a horcrux?

1227
01:55:26,736 --> 01:55:29,864
Yes, it was successful. And not just once.

1228
01:55:30,031 --> 01:55:31,074
What are they, exactly?

1229
01:55:31,240 --> 01:55:34,577
They can be anything,
very ordinary objects.

1230
01:55:37,747 --> 01:55:39,457
A ring, for example.

1231
01:55:40,083 --> 01:55:41,584
Or a book.

1232
01:55:42,877 --> 01:55:45,254
- Tom Riddle's Diary.
- It's a horcrux, yes.

1233
01:55:45,755 --> 01:55:47,882
4 years ago, when you saved
to Ginny Weasley...

1234
01:55:48,049 --> 01:55:50,343
...you brought me this.

1235
01:55:50,510 --> 01:55:52,428
I knew it was another kind of magic.

1236
01:55:52,595 --> 01:55:57,600
Very dark, very powerful.
But until today I didn't know how powerful.

1237
01:55:57,767 --> 01:55:59,769
- And the ring?
- From Voldemort's mother.

1238
01:56:00,144 --> 01:56:04,899
Hard to find.
Even harder to destroy.

1239
01:56:05,066 --> 01:56:08,945
But if you found them all,
If you destroyed every horcrux...

1240
01:56:09,112 --> 01:56:10,279
One would destroy Voldemort.

1241
01:56:10,446 --> 01:56:13,366
But how to find them?
They are hidden, right?

1242
01:56:13,533 --> 01:56:16,786
It's true. But the magic,
especially the dark one...

1243
01:56:30,758 --> 01:56:32,635
...leaves traces.

1244
01:56:40,435 --> 01:56:42,520
Is that where you go when you're away...

1245
01:56:42,687 --> 01:56:44,981
- ...from school?
- Yes.

1246
01:56:45,815 --> 01:56:48,901
And I think maybe I already found another one.

1247
01:56:49,068 --> 01:56:53,156
But this time I can't destroy it alone.

1248
01:56:54,699 --> 01:56:59,370
Again I must ask too much of you,
Harry.

1249
01:57:03,332 --> 01:57:05,626
Have you ever considered
you ask too much...

1250
01:57:05,793 --> 01:57:08,421
...that you assume too many things?

1251
01:57:08,588 --> 01:57:13,634
Has it crossed your bright head
I don't want to do this anymore?

1252
01:57:13,801 --> 01:57:15,928
What I thought is irrelevant.

1253
01:57:16,804 --> 01:57:22,602
I won't negotiate with you.
You agreed and it was over.

1254
01:57:40,995 --> 01:57:42,622
Harry.

1255
01:57:45,208 --> 01:57:47,543
You need to shave, my friend.

1256
01:57:50,338 --> 01:57:54,550
sometimes I forget
how much you have grown.

1257
01:57:54,717 --> 01:57:58,679
Sometimes I still see the child
small from the cupboard.

1258
01:58:00,223 --> 01:58:02,600
Forgive my sentimentality.

1259
01:58:03,059 --> 01:58:04,560
I'm old now.

1260
01:58:04,727 --> 01:58:06,395
I see it the same, sir.

1261
01:58:07,855 --> 01:58:10,858
Just like your mother, you are always kind.

1262
01:58:11,025 --> 01:58:14,237
A characteristic that people
does not value enough.

1263
01:58:16,989 --> 01:58:21,494
The place we travel to tonight
It is extremely dangerous.

1264
01:58:21,661 --> 01:58:25,164
I promised you could come with me
and I will keep my promise.

1265
01:58:25,331 --> 01:58:27,166
But with one condition:

1266
01:58:27,333 --> 01:58:30,545
You must obey all my orders,
without saying a word

1267
01:58:31,420 --> 01:58:33,047
Yes, sir.

1268
01:58:33,214 --> 01:58:35,341
Do you understand what I'm telling you?

1269
01:58:35,925 --> 01:58:38,427
If I tell you to hide, you hide.

1270
01:58:38,594 --> 01:58:40,930
If I tell you to run, you run.

1271
01:58:41,097 --> 01:58:45,101
If I tell you to abandon me and save yourself,
you have to do it.

1272
01:58:50,273 --> 01:58:51,857
Give me your word, Harry.

1273
01:58:53,484 --> 01:58:54,986
I give you my word.

1274
01:58:55,778 --> 01:58:57,446
Take my arm.

1275
01:58:58,864 --> 01:59:01,284
I believed that one could not
Apparate to Hogwarts.

1276
01:59:01,951 --> 01:59:05,413
I have my privileges.

1277
01:59:52,668 --> 01:59:54,295
This is the place.

1278
01:59:55,087 --> 01:59:56,672
Oh yes.

1279
01:59:57,590 --> 02:00:00,176
This place has known magic.

1280
02:00:08,184 --> 02:00:09,727
- Sir!
- In order to pass...

1281
02:00:09,894 --> 02:00:11,312
...one must make a payment.

1282
02:00:11,479 --> 02:00:15,107
A payment that weakens intruders.

1283
02:00:16,692 --> 02:00:18,527
- He should have left it to me.
- No.

1284
02:00:18,986 --> 02:00:21,697
Your blood is worth much more than mine.

1285
02:00:43,594 --> 02:00:48,224
Voldemort put obstacles in place so that
we would not find his hiding place.

1286
02:00:48,391 --> 02:00:51,727
Surely he put certain
defenses in place.

1287
02:00:54,313 --> 02:00:55,731
Be careful.

1288
02:01:19,255 --> 02:01:20,381
There it is.

1289
02:01:21,882 --> 02:01:24,593
The question is: How do we get there?

1290
02:01:46,782 --> 02:01:48,617
If you do me a favor.

1291
02:02:35,915 --> 02:02:38,334
Do you believe the horcrux is there, sir?

1292
02:02:38,959 --> 02:02:40,336
Oh yes.

1293
02:02:51,430 --> 02:02:53,015
You have to drink it.

1294
02:02:53,182 --> 02:02:56,018
You have to drink it all.

1295
02:02:56,852 --> 02:03:00,189
Do you remember the conditions
the ones I brought you with?

1296
02:03:00,356 --> 02:03:02,775
This potion can paralyze me.

1297
02:03:03,192 --> 02:03:04,860
It can make me forget what I'm doing here.

1298
02:03:05,653 --> 02:03:08,948
It can cause me so much
pain that implores you.

1299
02:03:09,198 --> 02:03:11,116
You can't listen to me.

1300
02:03:11,283 --> 02:03:14,829
You need to make sure
to continue taking it.

1301
02:03:14,995 --> 02:03:17,456
Even if you have me
than forcing me to take it.

1302
02:03:17,915 --> 02:03:20,042
- Understood?
- Why don't I take it?

1303
02:03:20,209 --> 02:03:25,631
Because I'm older,
smarter and much less valuable.

1304
02:03:29,552 --> 02:03:31,637
Cheers, Harry.

1305
02:03:47,778 --> 02:03:49,071
Professor!

1306
02:03:51,198 --> 02:03:52,741
Professor!

1307
02:03:59,081 --> 02:04:00,583
Harry.

1308
02:04:00,749 --> 02:04:03,252
Professor, do you hear me?

1309
02:04:04,545 --> 02:04:05,713
Professor!

1310
02:04:21,145 --> 02:04:22,271
No. Don't do it.

1311
02:04:22,438 --> 02:04:24,773
He has to take it, like he said.
Do you remember?

1312
02:04:34,033 --> 02:04:35,784
- Stop.
- It's going to stop, but...

1313
02:04:35,951 --> 02:04:40,497
- ...only if he keeps drinking.
- Please don't force me!

1314
02:04:40,664 --> 02:04:42,791
- Forgive me, sir.
- Please!

1315
02:04:42,958 --> 02:04:45,252
Kill me! Kill me!

1316
02:04:47,171 --> 02:04:48,255
It's my fault.

1317
02:04:49,924 --> 02:04:51,133
It's all my fault.

1318
02:04:52,968 --> 02:04:54,595
It's my fault.

1319
02:04:54,762 --> 02:04:58,140
Just one more, sir.
One more and I promise...

1320
02:04:58,807 --> 02:05:01,143
I promise to do what you say.

1321
02:05:01,310 --> 02:05:03,145
I promise you!

1322
02:05:04,188 --> 02:05:05,564
Please!

1323
02:05:29,713 --> 02:05:31,173
Harry.

1324
02:05:38,305 --> 02:05:39,348
Water.

1325
02:05:40,349 --> 02:05:41,475
Water.

1326
02:05:41,642 --> 02:05:43,435
Water.

1327
02:05:49,942 --> 02:05:51,735
You did it, sir.

1328
02:05:51,902 --> 02:05:53,362
Look.

1329
02:05:55,364 --> 02:05:56,615
Harry.

1330
02:05:57,992 --> 02:05:59,326
Water.

1331
02:06:01,078 --> 02:06:02,746
<i>Aguamenti!</i>

1332
02:06:02,955 --> 02:06:04,415
Water.

1333
02:06:40,576 --> 02:06:41,952
<i>Lumos.</i>

1334
02:07:10,397 --> 02:07:12,316
<i>Lumos maxima!</i>

1335
02:07:27,664 --> 02:07:28,791
<i>Sectumsempra!</i>

1336
02:07:28,957 --> 02:07:30,125
Harry.

1337
02:07:31,085 --> 02:07:32,711
Faint! Faint!

1338
02:08:31,895 --> 02:08:33,188
Harry.

1339
02:08:37,192 --> 02:08:39,528
<i>Partis temporus!</i>

1340
02:09:22,070 --> 02:09:25,199
Go home!
Don't wander around!

1341
02:10:06,031 --> 02:10:09,743
We need to take him to the hospital,
with Madam Pomfrey.

1342
02:10:12,162 --> 02:10:13,538
No.

1343
02:10:14,581 --> 02:10:17,251
With Severus.
I need Severus.

1344
02:10:17,417 --> 02:10:20,963
Wake him up. Tell him what happened.

1345
02:10:21,129 --> 02:10:22,798
Don't talk to anyone else.

1346
02:10:23,423 --> 02:10:25,634
With Severus, Harry.

1347
02:10:30,931 --> 02:10:33,350
Hide below.

1348
02:10:34,810 --> 02:10:37,813
Don't talk or let me see you
no one without my permission.

1349
02:10:37,980 --> 02:10:41,775
Whatever happens,
It is imperative that you stay down.

1350
02:10:42,567 --> 02:10:44,403
Obey me, Harry.

1351
02:10:47,864 --> 02:10:49,157
Trust me.

1352
02:10:50,909 --> 02:10:52,369
Trust me.

1353
02:11:12,931 --> 02:11:14,766
Good night, Draco.

1354
02:11:15,642 --> 02:11:19,187
What brings you here
on this beautiful spring night?

1355
02:11:19,354 --> 02:11:21,106
Who else is here? I heard him talk!

1356
02:11:21,273 --> 02:11:25,360
Sometimes I talk to myself.
I find it extremely useful.

1357
02:11:27,487 --> 02:11:30,324
Have you been questioning yourself, Draco?

1358
02:11:32,826 --> 02:11:34,286
Draco...

1359
02:11:34,953 --> 02:11:37,914
- ...you are not a murderer.
-How do you know what I am?

1360
02:11:38,081 --> 02:11:39,875
I have done horrible things.

1361
02:11:40,042 --> 02:11:44,171
How to Spell Katie Bell
so that I could wear a cursed necklace?

1362
02:11:44,338 --> 02:11:46,965
How to put a bottle
of poisoned mead?

1363
02:11:47,132 --> 02:11:48,717
Forgive me, Draco.

1364
02:11:48,884 --> 02:11:51,386
I feel like those attempts are so weak...

1365
02:11:51,553 --> 02:11:53,930
...that your intentions were not serious.

1366
02:11:54,097 --> 02:11:57,309
He trusts me! He chose me!

1367
02:12:01,229 --> 02:12:02,898
Then it will make things easier for you.

1368
02:12:03,065 --> 02:12:04,733
<i>Expelliarmus!</i>

1369
02:12:08,070 --> 02:12:10,739
Very good. Very good.

1370
02:12:12,157 --> 02:12:13,617
You are not alone.

1371
02:12:14,701 --> 02:12:15,744
There are others.

1372
02:12:17,788 --> 02:12:19,206
How?

1373
02:12:20,499 --> 02:12:23,168
The evanescent wardrobe we have.

1374
02:12:23,919 --> 02:12:26,296
- I've been fixing it.
- Let me guess.

1375
02:12:26,463 --> 02:12:29,424
He has a brother, a twin.

1376
02:12:29,591 --> 02:12:31,802
At Borgin and Burke's. They form a corridor.

1377
02:12:31,968 --> 02:12:33,762
How ingenious.

1378
02:12:34,429 --> 02:12:35,680
Draco...

1379
02:12:35,847 --> 02:12:41,937
...years ago I met a boy who took
many wrong decisions.

1380
02:12:42,854 --> 02:12:45,774
- Please let me help you.
- I don't want your help!

1381
02:12:46,566 --> 02:12:50,070
Don't you understand? I have to do this!

1382
02:12:51,279 --> 02:12:52,948
I have to kill him.

1383
02:12:53,573 --> 02:12:55,617
Or he's going to kill me.

1384
02:13:05,127 --> 02:13:08,755
Look what we have here.

1385
02:13:10,632 --> 02:13:12,801
Well done, Draco.

1386
02:13:16,471 --> 02:13:18,306
Good night, Bellatrix.

1387
02:13:19,349 --> 02:13:21,518
This calls for some introductions.

1388
02:13:21,685 --> 02:13:26,815
I would love to, but I'm afraid
that we have little time.

1389
02:13:27,441 --> 02:13:28,817
Do it!

1390
02:13:30,110 --> 02:13:34,239
He doesn't have the guts, just like his father.

1391
02:13:34,656 --> 02:13:36,158
Let me finish him off my way.

1392
02:13:36,324 --> 02:13:39,953
The Dark Lord said
that the boy had to do it.

1393
02:13:40,120 --> 02:13:42,164
This is your moment. Do it.

1394
02:13:43,707 --> 02:13:45,709
Come on, Draco!

1395
02:13:45,876 --> 02:13:48,044
Now!

1396
02:13:49,296 --> 02:13:50,630
No.

1397
02:14:02,517 --> 02:14:04,060
Severus.

1398
02:14:13,069 --> 02:14:14,529
Please.

1399
02:14:15,530 --> 02:14:16,865
<i>Avada Kedavra!</i>

1400
02:14:59,824 --> 02:15:03,078
Yes!

1401
02:15:21,263 --> 02:15:24,724
Hagrid! Hello?

1402
02:15:24,891 --> 02:15:28,937
Snape! He trusted you!

1403
02:15:33,275 --> 02:15:34,901
Go!

1404
02:15:35,569 --> 02:15:37,279
<i>Incarcerus!</i>

1405
02:15:37,445 --> 02:15:40,115
Defend yourself! Coward, defend yourself!

1406
02:15:41,741 --> 02:15:44,953
Nope! It belongs to the Dark Lord.

1407
02:16:05,098 --> 02:16:06,474
<i>Sectumsempra!</i>

1408
02:16:14,941 --> 02:16:20,196
Do you dare to use my own
spells against me?

1409
02:16:20,947 --> 02:16:22,115
Yes.

1410
02:16:22,824 --> 02:16:26,995
I am the Half-Blood Prince.

1411
02:20:15,056 --> 02:20:16,516
Potter...

1412
02:20:17,225 --> 02:20:19,727
...in view of what has happened...

1413
02:20:21,145 --> 02:20:24,440
...if you need to talk to someone...

1414
02:20:26,401 --> 02:20:30,405
you should know
that Professor Dumbledore...

1415
02:20:32,240 --> 02:20:34,701
He loved you very much.

1416
02:20:52,969 --> 02:20:54,846
Do you think he would have done it?

1417
02:20:55,430 --> 02:20:57,181
Draco?

1418
02:20:58,266 --> 02:20:59,601
No.

1419
02:21:00,768 --> 02:21:02,812
No, he was lowering his wand.

1420
02:21:03,855 --> 02:21:05,815
In the end, it was Snape.

1421
02:21:06,441 --> 02:21:08,318
It was always Snape.

1422
02:21:09,152 --> 02:21:10,945
And I didn't do anything.

1423
02:21:17,952 --> 02:21:19,370
It's not real.

1424
02:21:20,955 --> 02:21:22,290
Open it.

1425
02:21:33,301 --> 02:21:37,305
"To the Dark Lord. I know I will be
dead long before you read this...

1426
02:21:37,472 --> 02:21:40,767
...but I want you to know
that I discovered his secret.

1427
02:21:42,143 --> 02:21:46,022
I stole the real horcrux
and I will destroy it as soon as possible.

1428
02:21:46,189 --> 02:21:49,233
I face death hoping that when
meets his equal...

1429
02:21:49,400 --> 02:21:51,653
...you be mortal again.

1430
02:21:52,946 --> 02:21:54,614
R.A.B.”

1431
02:21:55,865 --> 02:21:57,325
R.A.B.

1432
02:21:57,700 --> 02:21:58,993
I don't know.

1433
02:22:00,995 --> 02:22:03,665
But they have the real horcrux.

1434
02:22:04,624 --> 02:22:06,167
It was all a big waste.

1435
02:22:07,502 --> 02:22:09,003
Everything.

1436
02:22:15,218 --> 02:22:17,303
Ron thinks that's fine.

1437
02:22:17,804 --> 02:22:19,305
You and Ginny.

1438
02:22:19,931 --> 02:22:23,643
But when he's around,
Give him a minimum of kisses.

1439
02:22:24,978 --> 02:22:26,980
I'm not coming back, Hermione.

1440
02:22:28,147 --> 02:22:30,858
I have to finish what I started
Dumbledore...

1441
02:22:31,025 --> 02:22:33,861
...and I don't know where it's going to take me...

1442
02:22:34,028 --> 02:22:37,657
...but I will inform you
and Ron where I am, when I can.

1443
02:22:38,992 --> 02:22:41,619
I've always admired your courage, Harry.

1444
02:22:41,786 --> 02:22:44,455
But sometimes you can be very stupid.

1445
02:22:47,500 --> 02:22:49,752
Do you think you will be able to find...

1446
02:22:49,919 --> 02:22:52,296
...all the horcruxes alone?

1447
02:22:56,551 --> 02:22:58,219
You need us, Harry.

1448
02:23:14,027 --> 02:23:17,113
I hadn't realized
how beautiful this place is.

1449
02:26:39,732 --> 02:26:42,026
HARRY POTTER
AND THE MYSTERY OF THE PRINCE
